ns used to generate a set of results included in the provenance records to link computational actions to particular environments?\nstamped-checklist:must/007\tmust\tA.1\tIs a `README.md` or `Makefile` included with instructions for installation and usage?\nstamped-checklist:must/008\tmust\tA.1\tIs there a clear starting point for users to start reproducing results (e.g., a main script, a workflow definition, or a container image)?\nstamped-checklist:must/009\tmust\tP.1\tAre relative paths used in scripts, avoiding hardcoded or system-specific paths like `C:\\Users\\...` or `/home/user/...`?\nstamped-checklist:must/010\tmust\tP.1\tAre all software dependencies included in the environment specification, rather than relying on pre-installed tools?\nstamped-checklist:must/011\tmust\tP.1\tHave all assumptions about the host system's configuration been documented (e.g., specific OS versions, required system libraries, or environment variables)?\nstamped-checklist:must/012\tmust\tP.2\tIs there a clear list of system requirements and dependencies documented in the README or environment specifications?\nstamped-checklist:must/013\tmust\tP.3\tAre environment specifications (e.g., Dockerfiles, `pyproject.toml`, `package.json`) included in the version control system alongside code and data?\nstamped-checklist:must/014\tmust\tP.3\tIs there a process for updating environment specifications when dependencies change, and are these updates tracked in version control?\nstamped-checklist:must/015\tmust\tD.1\tAre environment specifications (e.g., container digests, frozen package manifests) included to ensure others can attempt to exactly replicate the environment?\nstamped-checklist:must/016\tmust\tD.1\tAre environment specifications shared in a way that others can access and use them (e.g., published container images, archived environment files)?\nstamped-checklist:must/017\tmust\tD.1\tIs there documentation on how to obtain and use the environment specifications for reproduction?\nstamped-checklist:should/001\tshould\tT.2\tIs a common version control system (e.g., `Git`, DVC, `git-annex`, or DataLad) used across all components?\nstamped-checklist:should/002\tshould\tA.2\tIs the workflow tested regularly to ensure instructions remain accurate?\nstamped-checklist:should/003\tshould\tM.1\tAre raw data, processed data, code, and environment definitions separated into distinct modules?\nstamped-checklist:should/009\tshould\tM.4\tAre restricted data or software kept in their own modules?\nstamped-checklist:should/004\tshould\tE.1\tIs the pipeline tested in a fresh container, batch job, clean virtual machine, or cloud-based instance?\nstamped-checklist:should/005\tshould\tE.1\tDoes the workflow spawn disposable environments for each execution, allowing for isolation of runs?\nstamped-checklist:should/006\tshould\tD.2\tAre the exact environment specifications used to generate a specific set of results regularly tested to ensure they can be reconstituted as intended?\nstamped-checklist:should/007\tshould\tD.2\tAre environment artifacts archived within the research object where possible (e.g., executable binaries, container images)?\nstamped-checklist:should/008\tshould\tD.2\tIs there a process for updating environment specifications when dependencies change, and are these updates tracked in version control?\nstamped-checklist:may/001\tmay\tM.2\tAre external datasets or software dependencies included as submodules or linked as submodules?\nstamped-checklist:may/002\tmay\tM.2\tIs the modular structure documented to clarify how components relate and can be recombined?\nstamped-checklist:may/003\tmay\tM.2\tAre modular boundaries defined in a way that allows independent updates without breaking the overall workflow?\nstamped-checklist:may/004\tmay\tM.2\tIs there a clear mechanism for composing modules together (e.g., `git` submodules, or container orchestration)?\nstamped-checklist:may/005\tmay\tM.2\tIs there documentation or tooling to support users in understanding and navigating the modular structure?\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc 'cat > \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/replay-plan.md\" <<'\"'EOF'\n# Replay declaration (before the single attempt)\n\n**Documented entrypoint and exact command:** From the workspace root, run /Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/common-environment/.pixi/envs/default/bin/python analysis/analyze.py, exactly as stated in the worker README. The interpreter must exist and be executable; its NumPy, SciPy, pandas, NiBabel, Matplotlib and Nilearn imports must resolve as the README describes. The entrypoint uses only captured input maps, metadata, and local template files; no retrieval is initiated by the adapter or by the script.\n\n**Protected inputs and source:** The frozen helper will make a separate writable copy of the canonical original complete delivery. Participant maps, participant metadata, input/sources.json, the upstream methods, analysis code, and template images are protected. The inspection copy is not used for replay.\n\n**Explicit generated output selection (only these files may be removed/recreated in the replay copy):**\n- results/primary_v2_template_mask/group_mean_effect.nii.gz\n- results/primary_v2_template_mask/group_t_positive.nii.gz\n- results/primary_v2_template_mask/group_t_fwe05_positive.nii.gz\n- results/primary_v2_template_mask/p_fwe_maxT_positive.nii.gz\n- results/primary_v2_template_mask/input_qc.csv\n- results/primary_v2_template_mask/summary.json\n- results/primary_v2_template_mask/top20_positive_voxels.csv\n- results/primary_v2_template_mask/vmPFC_participant_summary.csv\n- results/primary_v2_template_mask/whole_brain_fwe_voxels.csv\n- figures/primary_v2_template_mask/group_t_map.png\n- figures/primary_v2_template_mask/vmPFC_participant_effects.png\n\nThis selection follows the output inventory in README and the writes in analysis/analyze.py; it excludes the supplied input tree and preserved pilot results/figures.\n\n**Comparison rule:** For numeric NIfTI arrays and numeric CSV/JSON result fields, compare captured and replayed values at relative tolerance 1e-6 (the frozen helper's setting), considering NaN masks and image geometry. Scientific agreement is defined by matching participant count, model/mask definitions, group mean and t maps, max-T corrected p map, significant-voxel selection, and vmPFC estimate/interval. Ignore timestamps, log text, prose, and serialization/formatting. The two PNGs are generated artifacts for visual consistency; pixel-level differences are not a scientific disagreement. One attempt, 7,200-second execution limit, helper max-get compatibility value 5 GB.\nEOF\ntest -x /Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/common-environment/.pixi/envs/default/bin/python\n{ printf 'COMMAND: %q %q fresh-rerun --path %q --entry %q --outputs [11 declared outputs] --workdir %q -o %q --rtol 1e-6 --timeout 7200 --max-get-gb 5\\\\n' \\\"\"'$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET\" '\"'/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/common-environment/.pixi/envs/default/bin/python analysis/analyze.py' \\\"\"'$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/replay-copy\" \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/replay-record.json\"; \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" fresh-rerun --path \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET\" --entry '\"'/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/common-environment/.pixi/envs/default/bin/python analysis/analyze.py' --outputs results/primary_v2_template_mask/group_mean_effect.nii.gz results/primary_v2_template_mask/group_t_positive.nii.gz results/primary_v2_template_mask/group_t_fwe05_positive.nii.gz results/primary_v2_template_mask/p_fwe_maxT_positive.nii.gz results/primary_v2_template_mask/input_qc.csv results/primary_v2_template_mask/summary.json results/primary_v2_template_mask/top20_positive_voxels.csv results/primary_v2_template_mask/vmPFC_participant_