r x in changes),\n \"metadata_logical_equivalence\":\"not established\"}\n(Path(os.environ[\"STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT\"])/\"integrity-comparison.json\").write_text(json.dumps(result,indent=2)+\"'\"\\\\n\\\")\nprint(json.dumps(result,indent=2))\nPY\n} > \\\"\"'$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/integrity-compare-corrected.txt\" 2>&1\ncat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/integrity-comparison.json\"'","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"checked_manifest_entries\": 1140,\n  \"change_count\": 1,\n  \"changes\": [\n    {\n      \"path\": \".git/annex/keysdb/db\",\n      \"change\": \"sha256\",\n      \"expected\": \"f6f8fd7af99434db59fadc6da021051789c6aaa271ebf878c54dafc6c9fde5ca\",\n      \"observed\": \"233c0be3e02857e0fbf47b00b8a94de3e9126529bee41b2491286aef7372be80\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"classified_operational_metadata_only\": true,\n  \"metadata_logical_equivalence\": \"not established\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc 'cat > \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/assessment-report.md\" <<'\"'EOF'\n# Independent assessment — NARPS Hypothesis 1 group analysis\n\n**Canonical delivery:** SHA-256 a870dc3c816f624dcd1ecd9e513fe56b76cf182e109a2f95963749235a4df8d7  \n**Captured HEAD:** d857ab1302d13cb660a7a044af07141f44bfa9ba  \n**Assessment scope:** Complete stopped workspace as captured, including untracked files; inspection used the operational copy. Original evidence citations below use this canonical capture identity and paths relative to content/workspace/.\n\n## Scientific assessment\n\n**Scientific adequacy: supported.** The report's no-support conclusion for a positive vmPFC gain effect is supported by a defensible group analysis and an appropriately corrected whole-brain test. The reported hypothesis outcome is “We found no support for a positive gain effect in vmPFC in the equal-indifference group under whole-brain familywise correction.” This is a conclusion about evidence under the specified model, not evidence that the true vmPFC effect is exactly zero.\n\nThe worker analyzed all 54 equal-indifference participants as independent second-level units, joined by participant ID to one map per person. The input COPEs are participant contrast estimates, not t/z statistics or signal change per currency unit; the supplied upstream methods say the gain regressor was mean-centered and variance-normalized and that separate gain/loss models were used. The report correctly limits interpretation to that conditional, fixed upstream estimand. Evidence: input/study-task.md (SHA-256 e92bf2e0c0db4cc49688cce9f9dfff8a236fc4ec151c09961719f49f31310cc8), input/upstream-methods.md (508d832c8787ed8303c3de101c2c76f40a3aa5dec53e6993dc2a49c4b7bcf90b), and scientific-report.md (9573bd34e4db368eb719e949095019e17dcaf345ab6d8ce5d442bab0378384d0).\n\nThe primary model is a one-sample t test across participants with a one-sided positive whole-brain max-T sign-flip permutation correction (9,999 sign patterns, fixed seed, FWE α=.05). Its exchangeability/symmetry assumption is stated. The mask uses the matching asymmetric MNI152NLin2009c brain mask resampled to the participant grid, intersected with finite nonzero support in every map; the report quantifies retained coverage (186,192/196,466 template-mask voxels, 94.8%) and the consequence that genuine zero estimates could be excluded. It checks map IDs, geometry, checksums and nonfinite values. The broad, explicit vmPFC midline box is used descriptively while the confirmatory decision remains whole-brain corrected. The report distinguishes a posterior whole-brain finding from vmPFC and states that missing participant variance maps limit precision modeling. Evidence: research-protocol.md (fd82723ae27072a2dc5c3077756192457bcbc11e9b9a80eb378c33af0a9541c3), analysis/analyze.py (a881abeea818018c57b767504d18472867da80fac8b13dd8a93d34d2a457dde2), and results/primary_v2_template_mask/summary.json (81e50cce17229e0eed5a518b845355616a167eec507e5b8696a4474d8d093488). The reported vmPFC mean is −0.0026 COPE units (95% t interval −0.0219 to 0.0167; n=54), with descriptive one-sided uncorrected p=.606; its most positive voxel has whole-brain max-T FWE p=.7742. No vmPFC voxel survives the stated whole-brain correction. The report therefore supports “no support” without treating a null result as proof of no effect.\n\n**Independent replay:** The frozen helper made a fresh copy of the complete canonical delivery, removed only the 11 declared primary generated artifacts, and ran the README entrypoint once. It exited 0 in 15.67 seconds; all 11 selected outputs were byte-identical to the captured outputs. No target repair or scientific-input retrieval occurred. The exact command, prerequisites, protected inputs, output list and comparison rule were declared before the attempt in replay-plan.md; the frozen record and stdout/stderr are in replay-record.json and replay-copy/.\n\n## STAMPED item attainment at worker stop\n\nAttainment below is separate from scientific adequacy and replay measurement availability. The worker-stop receipt (SHA-256 f5893d27e5a793fefd9e6f206399753c64f3efc45f362fb0d28b0f9b5ceac95d) identifies the same complete capture and HEAD. Git status at stop has the worker's README, analysis, protocol, report, figures and results untracked; the HEAD is the earlier supplied-input commit. The commit therefore does not track the worker's scientific code or outputs. The assessment gives no worker-practice credit for coordinator-supplied commits or annex setup.\n\n- **Self-contained and inputs:** One workspace root contains the supplied participant maps, metadata, code and derivatives. The captured paths resolve within that root. The input manifest records 54 map URLs/checksums plus the cohort and methods sources. No separately maintained software component or submodule was identified.\n- **Versioning and tracking:** Git exists, but the worker's complete scientific work was untracked at stop. This leaves the tracked repository incomplete and does not establish worker use of git-annex for the worker's outputs. The probe's “large in annex” result describes supplied input pointers and is not credited as worker action. The 54 source maps themselves are annex-backed in the captured state.\n- **Instructions and entrypoint:** README documents the analysis question, input inventory, output locations, dependencies and a direct Python entrypoint. The entrypoint exists and was replayed successfully. However the documented interpreter is an absolute path under the originating host's shared environment, not a portable setup command.\n- **Environment and portability:** No environment specification is included with the worker's code/results at stop. The report records package versions, and README names Python and libraries, but neither is an exact reconstructible dependency lock/specification. The absolute interpreter path is a host assumption. Environment linkage, exact environment reproduction, update process, and worker-side fresh-environment testing are not established.\n- **Modularity and reuse:** Inputs, code, external template assets, results and figures occupy distinct directories, but the worker did not track the code/results and did not document independent module interfaces or a composition/update mechanism. No restricted component was identified.\n- **Workflow checking:** There is a saved plotting failure note followed by a declared fix and successful completed outputs. This is useful incident documentation, but there is no evidence of regular or exact-environment automated testing.\n\nThe probe sweep is retained in probes/probes.json; its draft was manually reviewed because it only scans tracked files and therefore misses worker-created untracked README, code and report. In particular, its entrypoint and environment findings were corrected from direct inspection. Probe statements about supplied annex pointers were not treated as evidence of worker annex actions.\n\n## Access and retrieval route\n\nThe intended recipient is a researcher using the worker-declared source URLs with network access; anonymous access is not a requirement. The route covers all 54 participant maps through the declared NeuroVault collection/media URLs, participant metadata through the pinned raw GitHub URL, and the two local TemplateFlow template assets through their declared S3 URLs. input/sources.json and the README identify the route and checksums. HEAD requests returned HTTP 200 for a sample map and NeuroVault collection API, the pinned cohort TSV, and the TemplateFlow mask and T1. This tests those hosts and representative objects; it does not test every map URL or establish a persistent mirror. See access-record.md and the per-request transcripts in access/. The coordinator's copy to the assessor is not counted as worker publication.\n\n## Integrity, attribution and limitations\n\nThe operational manifest matched the canonical manifest before inspection. After inspection, the only observed operational-copy difference was .git/annex/keysdb/db, a regular file in the specifically classified operational-metadata set; its hash changed during Git inspection. The other 1,139 checked entries, including all scientific files and links, matched. Logical database equivalence is not established, and the annex DB change is inspection-induced metadata, not worker evidence. The initial comparison script used the wrong manifest key for symlink targets and falsely listed input links; that failed attempt is retained in commands/integrity-compare.txt. A corrected comparison using link_target is retained in commands/integrity-compare-corrected.txt and recorded in integrity-comparison.json.\n\nThe capture contains .entire/ session material and .codex/hooks.json; their contents were not inspected or used as grading evidence. Supplied coordinator skill material has external reference limits in judge-target.json; no such original absolute/external pointer was followed. No treatment assignment was inferred. The replay environment overlay disabled Git hooks only in its disposable copy; the captured configuration was not edited. The helper completed without an assessor malfunction. The scientific conclusion remains conditional on supplied AO86 maps, their upstream modeling, the common-support choice, the stated symmetry assumption and the specified anatomical vmPFC box.\nEOF\ncat > \\\"\"'$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/access-record.md\" <<'\"'EOF'\n# Access route record\n\n- **Intended recipient:** Researcher using the worker-declared authorized source route with network access; anonymous access is not required.\n- **Declared route:** input/sources.json lists NeuroVault URLs for all 54 participant maps and the collection API; a pinned raw GitHub URL for participants.tsv; the README and result summary identify the TemplateFlow S3 URLs for the local MNI152NLin2009cAsym brain mask and T1.\n- **Required coverage:** 54 participant gain-effect maps, cohort metadata, and two template files. Upstream methods are linked to a pinned source in the manifest; the relevant methods are also retained locally.\n- **Tested host scope:** HEAD requests returned HTTP 200 for representative NeuroVault media/API, raw.githubusercontent.com cohort TSV, and both TemplateFlow S3 assets. This is representative-host testing, not a check of all 54 map URLs or a guarantee of future availability.\n- **Attribution:** These retrieval links are present in the worker's stopped workspace. The coordinator's delivery copy is not treated as worker publication. No persistent worker-hosted mirror or authentication requirement is documented.\n- Raw command transcripts: access/neurovault-map.txt, access/neurovault-api.txt, access/github-cohort.txt, access/templateflow-mask.txt, access/templateflow-t1.txt.\nEOF\n\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc 'cat > \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/assessment-report.md\" <<'\"'EOF'\n# Independent assessment — NARPS Hypothesis 1 group analysis\n\n**Canonical delivery:** SHA-256 a870dc3c816f624dcd1ecd9e513fe56b76cf182e109a2f95963749235a4df8d7  \n**Captured HEAD:** d857ab1302d13cb660a7a044af07141f44bfa9ba  \n**Assessment scope:** Complete stopped workspace as captured, including untracked files; inspection used the operational copy. Original evidence citations below use this canonical capture identity and paths relative to content/workspace/.\n\n## Scientific assessment\n\n**Scientific adequacy: supported.** The report's no-support conclusion for a positive vmPFC gain effect is supported by a defensible group analysis and an appropriately corrected whole-brain test. The reported hypothesis outcome is “We found no support for a positive gain effect in vmPFC in the equal-indifference group under whole-brain familywise correction.” This is a conclusion about evidence under the specified model, not evidence that the true vmPFC effect is exactly zero.\n\nThe worker analyzed all 54 equal-indifference participants as independent second-level units, joined by participant ID to one map per person. The input COPEs are participant contrast estimates, not t/z statistics or signal change per currency unit; the supplied upstream methods say the gain regressor was mean-centered and variance-normalized and that separate gain/loss models were used. The report correctly limits interpretation to that conditional, fixed upstream estimand. Evidence: input/study-task.md (SHA-256 e92bf2e0c0db4cc49688cce9f9dfff8a236fc4ec151c09961719f49f31310cc8), input/upstream-methods.md (508d832c8787ed8303c3de101c2c76f40a3aa5dec53e6993dc2a49c4b7bcf90b), and scientific-report.md (9573bd34e4db368eb719e949095019e17dcaf345ab6d8ce5d442bab0378384d0).\n\nThe primary model is a one-sample t test across participants with a one-sided positive whole-brain max-T sign-flip permutation correction (9,999 sign patterns, fixed seed, FWE α=.05). Its exchangeability/symmetry assumption is stated. The mask uses the matching asymmetric MNI152NLin2009c brain mask resampled to the participant grid, intersected with finite nonzero support in every map; the report quantifies retained coverage (186,192/196,466 template-mask voxels, 94.8%) and the consequence that genuine zero estimates could be excluded. It checks map IDs, geometry, checksums and nonfinite values. The broad, explicit vmPFC midline box is used descriptively while the confirmatory decision remains whole-brain corrected. The report distinguishes a posterior whole-brain finding from vmPFC and states that missing participant variance maps limit precision modeling. Evidence: research-protocol.md (fd82723ae27072a2dc5c3077756192457bcbc11e9b9a80eb378c33af0a9541c3), analysis/analyze.py (a881abeea818018c57b767504d18472867da80fac8b13dd8a93d34d2a457dde2), and results/primary_v2_template_mask/summary.json (81e50cce17229e0eed5a518b845355616a167eec507e5b8696a4474d8d093488). The reported vmPFC mean is −0.0026 COPE units (95% t interval −0.0219 to 0.0167; n=54), with descriptive one-sided uncorrected p=.606; its most positive voxel has whole-brain max-T FWE p=.7742. No vmPFC voxel survives the stated whole-brain correction. The report therefore supports “no support” without treating a null result as proof of no effect.\n\n**Independent replay:** The frozen helper made a fresh copy of the complete canonical delivery, removed only the 11 declared primary generated artifacts, and ran the README entrypoint once. It exited 0 in 15.67 seconds; all 11 selected outputs were byte-identical to the captured outputs. No target repair or scientific-input retrieval occurred. The exact command, prerequisites, protected inputs, output list and comparison rule were declared before the attempt in replay-plan.md; the frozen record and stdout/stderr are in replay-record.json and replay-copy/.\n\n## STAMPED item attainment at worker stop\n\nAttainment below is separate from scientific adequacy and replay measurement availability. The worker-stop receipt (SHA-256 f5893d27e5a793fefd9e6f206399753c64f3efc45f362fb0d28b0f9b5ceac95d) identifies the same complete capture and HEAD. Git status at stop has the worker's README, analysis, protocol, report, figures and results untracked; the HEAD is the earlier supplied-input commit. The commit therefore does not track the worker's scientific code or outputs. The assessment gives no worker-practice credit for coordinator-supplied commits or annex setup.\n\n- **Self-contained and inputs:** One workspace root contains the supplied participant maps, metadata, code and derivatives. The captured paths resolve within that root. The input manifest records 54 map URLs/checksums plus the cohort and methods sources. No separately maintained software component or submodule was identified.\n- **Versioning and tracking:** Git exists, but the worker's complete scientific work was untracked at stop. This leaves the tracked repository incomplete and does not establish worker use of git-annex for the worker's outputs. The probe's “large in annex” result describes supplied input pointers and is not credited as worker action. The 54 source maps themselves are annex-backed in the captured state.\n- **Instructions and entrypoint:** README documents the analysis question, input inventory, output locations, dependencies and a direct Python entrypoint. The entrypoint exists and was replayed successfully. However the documented interpreter is an absolute path under the originating host's shared environment, not a portable setup command.\n- **Environment and portability:** No environment specification is included with the worker's code/results at stop. The report records package versions, and README names Python and libraries, but neither is an exact reconstructible dependency lock/specification. The absolute interpreter path is a host assumption. Environment linkage, exact environment reproduction, update process, and worker-side fresh-environment testing are not established.\n- **Modularity and reuse:** Inputs, code, external template assets, results and figures occupy distinct directories, but the worker did not track the code/results and did not document independent module interfaces or a composition/update mechanism. No restricted component was identified.\n- **Workflow checking:** There is a saved plotting failure note followed by a declared fix and successful completed outputs. This is useful incident documentation, but there is no evidence of regular or exact-environment automated testing.\n\nThe probe sweep is retained in probes/probes.json; its draft was manually reviewed because it only scans tracked files and therefore misses worker-created untracked README, code and report. In particular, its entrypoint and environment findings were corrected from direct inspection. Probe statements about supplied annex pointers were not treated as evidence of worker annex actions.\n\n## Access and retrieval route\n\nThe intended recipient is a researcher using the worker-declared source URLs with network access; anonymous access is not a requirement. The route covers all 54 participant maps through the declared NeuroVault collection/media URLs, participant metadata through the pinned raw GitHub URL, and the two local TemplateFlow template assets through their declared S3 URLs. input/sources.json and the README identify the route and checksums. HEAD requests returned HTTP 200 for a sample map and NeuroVault collection API, the pinned cohort TSV, and the TemplateFlow mask and T1. This tests those hosts and representative objects; it does not test every map URL or establish a persistent mirror. See access-record.md and the per-request transcripts in access/. The coordinator's copy to the assessor is not counted as worker publication.\n\n## Integrity, attribution and limitations\n\nThe operational manifest matched the canonical manifest before inspection. After inspection, the only observed operational-copy difference was .git/annex/keysdb/db, a regular file in the specifically classified operational-metadata set; its hash changed during Git inspection. The other 1,139 checked entries, including all scientific files and links, matched. Logical database equivalence is not established, and the annex DB change is inspection-induced metadata, not worker evidence. The initial comparison script used the wrong manifest key for symlink targets and falsely listed input links; that failed attempt is retained in commands/integrity-compare.txt. A corrected comparison using link_target is retained in commands/integrity-compare-corrected.txt and recorded in integrity-comparison.json.\n\nThe capture contains .entire/ session material and .codex/hooks.json; their contents were not inspected or used as grading evidence. Supplied coordinator skill material has external reference limits in judge-target.json; no such original absolute/external pointer was followed. No treatment assignment was inferred. The replay environment overlay disabled Git hooks only in its disposable copy; the captured configuration was not edited. The helper completed without an assessor malfunction. The scientific conclusion remains conditional on supplied AO86 maps, their upstream modeling, the common-support choice, the stated symmetry assumption and the specified anatomical vmPFC box.\nEOF\ncat > \\\"\"'$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/access-record.md\" <<'\"'EOF'\n# Access route record\n\n- **Intended recipient:** Researcher using the worker-declared authorized source route with network access; anonymous access is not required.\n- **Declared route:** input/sources.json lists NeuroVault URLs for all 54 participant maps and the collection API; a pinned raw GitHub URL for participants.tsv; the README and result summary identify the TemplateFlow S3 URLs for the local MNI152NLin2009cAsym brain mask and T1.\n- **Required coverage:** 54 participant gain-effect maps, cohort metadata, and two template files. Upstream methods are linked to a pinned source in the manifest; the relevant methods are also retained locally.\n- **Tested host scope:** HEAD requests returned HTTP 200 for representative NeuroVault media/API, raw.githubusercontent.com cohort TSV, and both TemplateFlow S3 assets. This is representative-host testing, not a check of all 54 map URLs or a guarantee of future availability.\n- **Attribution:** These retrieval links are present in the worker's stopped workspace. The coordinator's delivery copy is not treated as worker publication. No persistent worker-hosted mirror or authentication requirement is documented.\n- Raw command transcripts: access/neurovault-map.txt, access/neurovault-api.txt, access/github-cohort.txt, access/templateflow-mask.txt, access/templateflow-t1.txt.\nEOF\n\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc '\"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" - <<'\"'PY'\nimport json, os\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path(os.environ[\\\"STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT\\\"])/\\\"response.json\\\"\nd=json.loads(p.read_text())\ncap=\\\"a870dc3c816f624dcd1ecd9e513fe56b76cf182e109a2f95963749235a4df8d7\\\"\nfiles={\n \\\"README.md\\\":\\\"b3962989dd4f90de42176285182bf88cf9ea6dc72698fe28237d5de2b872f97e\\\",\n \\\"analysis/analyze.py\\\":\\\"a881abeea818018c57b767504d18472867da80fac8b13dd8a93d34d2a457dde2\\\",\n \\\"input/sources.json\\\":\\\"919be9b4278c31f7e39ae3d02fcf159eb4ae222a2fb96c90df7c3a92e5fb19cd\\\",\n \\\"scientific-report.md\\\":\\\"9573bd34e4db368eb719e949095019e17dcaf345ab6d8ce5d442bab0378384d0\\\",\n \\\"research-protocol.md\\\":\\\"fd82723ae27072a2dc5c3077756192457bcbc11e9b9a80eb378c33af0a9541c3\\\",\n \\\"input/upstream-methods.md\\\":\\\"508d832c8787ed8303c3de101c2c76f40a3aa5dec53e6993dc2a49c4b7bcf90b\\\",\n \\\"results/primary_v2_template_mask/summary.json\\\":\\\"81e50cce17229e0eed5a518b845355616a167eec507e5b8696a4474d8d093488\\\",\n}\ndef ev(path, desc):\n sha=files.get(path)\n return {\\\"uri\\\":f\\\"capture:{cap}:content/workspace/{path}\\\",\\\"description\\\":desc,\\\"sha256\\\":sha}\ndef dir_ev(desc):\n return {\\\"uri\\\":f\\\"capture:{cap}:content/workspace/\\\",\\\"description\\\":desc,\\\"sha256\\\":None}\ndef setv(item,status,reason,evidence):\n key=\\\"stamped-checklist:\\\"+item\n r=d[\\\"responses\\\"][key]\n r.update({\\\"value\\\": \\\"yes\\\" if status==\\\"met\\\" else (\\\"no\\\" if status in (\\\"unmet\\\",\\\"partial\\\") else None),\n           \\\"reason\\\":reason,\\\"status\\\":status,\\\"evidence\\\":evidence,\\\"source\\\":\\\"judgement\\\",\\\"flags\\\":[]})\nsetv(\\\"must/001\\\",\\\"met\\\",\\\"All captured workspace content is under the workspace root; participant links resolve within its Git annex tree.\\\",[ev(\\\"input/sources.json\\\",\\\"Input inventory and source paths are within the common workspace.\\\")])\nsetv(\\\"must/002\\\",\\\"met\\\",\\\"The maps, metadata and analysis inputs are present under the common root; the manifest records reachable retrieval URLs and checksums.\\\",[ev(\\\"input/sources.json\\\",\\\"54 map entries and pinned metadata/methods retrieval references.\\\")])\nsetv(\\\"must/003\\\",\\\"unmet\\\",\\\"Python and scientific libraries are external runtime dependencies; no environment specification or software submodule is included at worker stop.\\\",[ev(\\\"README.md\\\",\\\"README lists Python and dependencies but depends on a pre-existing external interpreter.\\\"),dir_ev(\\\"Complete workspace inventory has no tracked environment specification or software submodule.\\\")])\nsetv(\\\"must/004\\\",\\\"unmet\\\",\\\"The worker's code, documentation, figures and results were untracked at stop; the captured HEAD is the supplied-input commit.\\\",[ev(\\\"analysis/analyze.py\\\",\\\"Scientific code is present but untracked at worker stop.\\\"),ev(\\\"scientific-report.md\\\",\\\"Scientific report is present but untracked at worker stop.\\\")])\nsetv(\\\"must/005\\\",\\\"unmet\\\",\\\"Captured inputs use annex pointers, but these were supplied in the baseline; the worker's generated image outputs were left untracked and no worker annex action is evidenced.\\\",[ev(\\\"results/primary_v2_template_mask/summary.json\\\",\\\"Generated NIfTI outputs/provenance exist as worker results outside tracked HEAD.\\\"),ev(\\\"README.md\\\",\\\"README identifies generated binary outputs; worker stop status leaves outputs untracked.\\\")])\nsetv(\\\"must/006\\\",\\\"unmet\\\",\\\"The summary records package versions and a command, but no exact environment specification is linked to the results.\\\",[ev(\\\"results/primary_v2_template_mask/summary.json\\\",\\\"Software versions and command are recorded, but no lock/specification identity.\\\"),dir_ev(\\\"No worker environment specification exists in the captured workspace.\\\")])\nsetv(\\\"must/007\\\",\\\"partial\\\",\\\"README explains usage and names dependencies but gives no portable installation/setup procedure; it assumes an absolute pre-existing interpreter.\\\",[ev(\\\"README.md\\\",\\\"Run instructions and package list are present; interpreter path is host-specific.\\\")])\nsetv(\\\"must/008\\\",\\\"met\\\",\\\"README identifies analysis/analyze.py as the starting point; the documented command completed in the one permitted replay.\\\",[ev(\\\"README.md\\\",\\\"Documented direct entrypoint.\\\"),ev(\\\"analysis/analyze.py\\\",\\\"Runnable group-analysis script.\\\")])\nsetv(\\\"must/009\\\",\\\"unmet\\\",\\\"The README and provenance command hard-code an absolute interpreter path, despite relative paths inside the analysis script.\\\",[ev(\\\"README.md\\\",\\\"Absolute interpreter path in usage command.\\\"),ev(\\\"results/primary_v2_template_mask/summary.json\\\",\\\"Absolute command recorded in provenance.\\\")])\nsetv(\\\"must/010\\\",\\\"unmet\\\",\\\"Dependencies are named in README but no environment specification declares and resolves them.\\\",[ev(\\\"README.md\\\",\\\"Named packages without an installable environment spec.\\\"),dir_ev(\\\"No lockfile, container definition or project package manifest at worker stop.\\\")])\nsetv(\\\"must/011\\\",\\\"partial\\\",\\\"README names Python 3.13.16 and a pre-existing shared interpreter, but does not fully document host/system requirements or setup assumptions.\\\",[ev(\\\"README.md\\\",\\\"Runtime version is stated, interpreter assumes the originating host path.\\\")])\nsetv(\\\"must/012\\\",\\\"partial\\\",\\\"The README lists Python and libraries, but omits portable installation details and a complete system requirements list.\\\",[ev(\\\"README.md\\\",\\\"Dependency names are present; no reproducible system/setup declaration.\\\")])\nsetv(\\\"must/013\\\",\\\"unmet\\\",\\\"No environment specification is included in version control at worker stop.\\\",[dir_ev(\\\"Complete captured workspace inventory contains no environment specification; worker outputs are untracked.\\\")])\nsetv(\\\"must/014\\\",\\\"unmet\\\",\\\"No environment update process or tracked environment changes are documented.\\\",[dir_ev(\\\"No environment specification or update record is present at worker stop.\\\")])\nsetv(\\\"must/015\\\",\\\"unmet\\\",\\\"Package versions alone do not provide an exact environment specification for reconstruction.\\\",[ev(\\\"results/primary_v2_template_mask/summary.json\\\",\\\"Version list without a lockfile/container digest.\\\")])\nsetv(\\\"must/016\\\",\\\"unmet\\\",\\\"No worker environment specification is present to share.\\\",[dir_ev(\\\"No environment artifact or specification in captured workspace.\\\")])\nsetv(\\\"must/017\\\",\\\"unmet\\\",\\\"There are no environment specifications to obtain or use; README assumes an externally prepared interpreter.\\\",[ev(\\\"README.md\\\",\\\"The documented run command uses an existing absolute interpreter.\\\")])\nsetv(\\\"should/001\\\",\\\"partial\\\",\\\"Git tracks the supplied input baseline, but the worker's analysis code, report and derived results were untracked at stop.\\\",[ev(\\\"analysis/analyze.py\\\",\\\"Untracked worker code.\\\"),ev(\\\"scientific-report.md\\\",\\\"Untracked worker report.\\\")])\nsetv(\\\"should/002\\\",\\\"not-checked\\\",\\\"One recorded plotting failure and completed rerun do not establish regular testing frequency.\\\",[ev(\\\"README.md\\\",\\\"No recurring test schedule is documented.\\\")])\nsetv(\\\"should/003\\\",\\\"partial\\\",\\\"Inputs, code, external assets, results and figures have separate directories; no tracked environment module or explicit modular interfaces exist.\\\",[ev(\\\"README.md\\\",\\\"Directory/output layout is described.\\\"),ev(\\\"research-protocol.md\\\",\\\"Inputs and analysis responsibilities are described.\\\")])\nsetv(\\\"should/009\\\",\\\"not-applicable\\\",\\\"No restricted data or software component is identified in the captured workspace.\\\",[ev(\\\"input/sources.json\\\",\\\"Public source URLs and data inventory.\\\")])\nsetv(\\\"should/004\\\",\\\"not-checked\\\",\\\"The evaluator replay is not worker practice; no worker-side clean container/VM test is documented.\\\",[ev(\\\"README.md\\\",\\\"No fresh-environment test record.\\\")])\nsetv(\\\"should/005\\\",\\\"not-checked\\\",\\\"No worker evidence establishes disposable isolation for executions.\\\",[dir_ev(\\\"No worker environment or run isolation record is present.\\\")])\nsetv(\\\"should/006\\\",\\\"not-checked\\\",\\\"No exact environment specification exists whose recurring reconstitution could be checked.\\\",[dir_ev(\\\"No environment specification or reconstitution record is present.\\\")])\nsetv(\\\"should/007\\\",\\\"unmet\\\",\\\"No environment artifact is archived in the worker's research object.\\\",[dir_ev(\\\"No environment archive/image or lockfile is present.\\\")])\nsetv(\\\"should/008\\\",\\\"unmet\\\",\\\"No tracked process for updating environment specifications is documented.\\\",[dir_ev(\\\"No environment specification or update procedure is present.\\\")])\nsetv(\\\"may/001\\\",\\\"unmet\\\",\\\"The dataset is included through supplied annex pointers and external software is not linked as a submodule.\\\",[ev(\\\"input/sources.json\\\",\\\"External dataset provenance is URL-based; no software submodule is described.\\\")])\nsetv(\\\"may/002\\\",\\\"partial\\\",\\\"README documents major directories and outputs, but does not describe module relationships or recombination.\\\",[ev(\\\"README.md\\\",\\\"Directory and output overview.\\\")])\nsetv(\\\"may/003\\\",\\\"partial\\\",\\\"Input/code/output directories are distinguishable, but independent update boundaries and interfaces are not described.\\\",[ev(\\\"research-protocol.md\\\",\\\"Analysis protocol identifies inputs and outputs without modular interface rules.\\\")])\nsetv(\\\"may/004\\\",\\\"unmet\\\",\\\"No submodule, orchestration or other module-composition mechanism is documented.\\\",[ev(\\\"README.md\\\",\\\"Direct entrypoint is documented; no module composition mechanism.\\\")])\nsetv(\\\"may/005\\\",\\\"met\\\",\\\"README and research protocol give readers an entrypoint, input map inventory, outputs and method structure.\\\",[ev(\\\"README.md\\\",\\\"Usage and output map.\\\"),ev(\\\"research-protocol.md\\\",\\\"Method and input/output description.\\\")])\nd[\\\"object\\\"]={\\\"url\\\":None,\\\"commit\\\":\\\"d857ab1302d13cb660a7a044af07141f44bfa9ba\\\",\\\"captured_at\\\":\\\"2026-10-16T06:48:11.174906+00:00\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"study\\\"}\nd[\\\"scope\\\"]=\\\"Inspection of the complete canonical stopped delivery via its operational copy; one frozen complete-delivery replay, representative route checks, and manual item judgments. Worker stop attribution applied; no treatment assignment inferred.\\\"\nd[\\\"assessor\\\"].update({\\\"skill\\\":\\\"assess-alignment-with-stamped-principles\\\",\\\"version\\\":\\\"0.1.0\\\",\\\"date\\\":\\\"2026-10-16\\\",\\\"drafted_by\\\":\\\"independent-judgement\\\"})\np.write_text(json.dumps(d,indent=2)+\\\"\\\\n\\\")\nPY\n{ printf 'COMMAND: assessment runner response stamp --capture canonical manifest; then validate and encode\\\\n'; \\\"\"'$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" response stamp \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/response.json\" --harness \"frozen external assessor\" --model \"Codex GPT-6\" --scope \"complete stopped delivery, operational inspection, one replay\" --kind study --capture \"$STAMPED_DELIVERY_MANIFEST\"; \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" response validate \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/response.json\"; \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" response encode \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/response.json\"; } > \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/response-validation-and-link.txt\" 2>&1\ncat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/response-validation-and-link.txt\"'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc '\"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" - <<'\"'PY'\nimport json, os\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path(os.environ[\\\"STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT\\\"])/\\\"response.json\\\"\nd=json.loads(p.read_text())\ncap=\\\"a870dc3c816f624dcd1ecd9e513fe56b76cf182e109a2f95963749235a4df8d7\\\"\nfiles={\n \\\"README.md\\\":\\\"b3962989dd4f90de42176285182bf88cf9ea6dc72698fe28237d5de2b872f97e\\\",\n \\\"analysis/analyze.py\\\":\\\"a881abeea818018c57b767504d18472867da80fac8b13dd8a93d34d2a457dde2\\\",\n \\\"input/sources.json\\\":\\\"919be9b4278c31f7e39ae3d02fcf159eb4ae222a2fb96c90df7c3a92e5fb19cd\\\",\n \\\"scientific-report.md\\\":\\\"9573bd34e4db368eb719e949095019e17dcaf345ab6d8ce5d442bab0378384d0\\\",\n \\\"research-protocol.md\\\":\\\"fd82723ae27072a2dc5c3077756192457bcbc11e9b9a80eb378c33af0a9541c3\\\",\n \\\"input/upstream-methods.md\\\":\\\"508d832c8787ed8303c3de101c2c76f40a3aa5dec53e6993dc2a49c4b7bcf90b\\\",\n \\\"results/primary_v2_template_mask/summary.json\\\":\\\"81e50cce17229e0eed5a518b845355616a167eec507e5b8696a4474d8d093488\\\",\n}\ndef ev(path, desc):\n sha=files.get(path)\n return {\\\"uri\\\":f\\\"capture:{cap}:content/workspace/{path}\\\",\\\"description\\\":desc,\\\"sha256\\\":sha}\ndef dir_ev(desc):\n return {\\\"uri\\\":f\\\"capture:{cap}:content/workspace/\\\",\\\"description\\\":desc,\\\"sha256\\\":None}\ndef setv(item,status,reason,evidence):\n key=\\\"stamped-checklist:\\\"+item\n r=d[\\\"responses\\\"][key]\n r.update({\\\"value\\\": \\\"yes\\\" if status==\\\"met\\\" else (\\\"no\\\" if status in (\\\"unmet\\\",\\\"partial\\\") else None),\n           \\\"reason\\\":reason,\\\"status\\\":status,\\\"evidence\\\":evidence,\\\"source\\\":\\\"judgement\\\",\\\"flags\\\":[]})\nsetv(\\\"must/001\\\",\\\"met\\\",\\\"All captured workspace content is under the workspace root; participant links resolve within its Git annex tree.\\\",[ev(\\\"input/sources.json\\\",\\\"In