{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc \"{ printf 'COMMAND: %q %q validate %q\\\\n' \\\"\"'$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/response.json\"; \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" validate \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/response.json\"; } > \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/frozen-response-validation.txt\" 2>&1\n\"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" - <<'\"'PY'\nimport os,re\nfrom pathlib import Path\nroot=Path(os.environ[\\\"STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT\\\"])\nlog=(root/\\\"commands/response-validation-and-link-final.txt\\\").read_text()\nurl=re.search(r\\\"https://checklist\\\\.stamped-principles\\\\.org/\\\\?[\"'^'\"\\\\s]+\\\",log)\nif not url: raise SystemExit(\\\"checklist link not found\\\")\n(root/\\\"checklist-link.md\\\").write_text(url.group(0)+\\\"\\\\n\\\")\nPY\ncat > \\\"\"'$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/command-index.md\" <<'\"'EOF'\n# Command and output index\n\nAll retained commands were run with the inherited GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0, annex.merge-annex-branches=false and annex.alwayscommit=false settings. Target inspections used only STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET (the operational copy); replay used the frozen helper's separate copy. No command ran in the canonical capture.\n\n- Required frozen runner check: commands/runner-check.txt (the initial required check also passed; a subsequent check with the same command is fully captured here).\n- Frozen probe sweep: commands/probes.txt; generated probes/probes.json and response.json.\n- Runner and response help/inventory discovery: output was shown during the assessment; key definitions are retained in probes/probes.json and the final checklist response.\n- Scientific document/code inspection: read-only reads from operational README, protocol, scientific report, summary, attempt note, study task, upstream methods and analysis script. Key evidence is cited by original capture path and SHA-256 in assessment-report.md; the full worker artifacts remain in the capture.\n- Git stop-state inspection: operational-copy git status --short --branch, git rev-parse HEAD, git remote -v, and git log -1 --oneline --decorate; results are summarized in assessment-report.md and the probe JSON. The commands ran with optional locks disabled.\n- First post-inspection inventory comparison: commands/integrity-compare.txt (failed comparison implementation; it used target rather than manifest link_target for symlinks, retained without relying on its false positives).\n- Corrected operational inventory comparison: commands/integrity-compare-corrected.txt and integrity-comparison.json; only .git/annex/keysdb/db differed.\n- Declared replay: commands/replay.txt, replay-plan.md, replay-record.json, replay-copy/replay.stdout and replay-copy/replay.stderr. The frozen helper completed with output match.\n- Access route checks: access/*.txt each preserve the URL, command, stdout and stderr.\n- Response validation attempts: commands/response-validation-and-link.txt and commands/response-validation-and-link-retry.txt preserve failed schema checks; commands/response-validation-and-link-final.txt is the successful validator and encoder output; commands/frozen-response-validation.txt is the frozen top-level runner validation.\n- Scientific record validation: commands/scientific-validation.txt preserves command and validator output.\nEOF\ncat \\\"\"'$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/frozen-response-validation.txt\"\ncat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/checklist-link.md\"'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
